{
    "background_story": "Janelle was a brilliant and eccentric botanist who spent most of her life studying the unique properties of plants. Her fascination with the dogbane plant, known for its toxic sap, led her to develop a groundbreaking medicine that could cure a previously incurable disease. As she delved deeper into her research, Janelle became increasingly reclusive, shutting herself away in her laboratory surrounded by specimens of the dogbane plant. Her colleagues would often joke that she was as poisonous as the plant itself, due to her sharp tongue and high standards. Despite her prickly demeanor, Janelle's discovery revolutionized the medical field, earning her a Nobel Prize and cementing her legacy as a pioneering scientist.",
